# Test: enum-refusal-daemon-start
#
# QUESTION: does the daemon's own config load refuse an enum value outside the
# enumeration in a hierarchical file with the same operator error
# `ze config validate` prints, after `error: load config:` and one
# `parse config:`, and exit 1 before any session? A unit test reaches the
# parser; only the daemon's start path proves the loader wraps the refusal
# once and keeps `fix:` as the last line.
#
# The set-format file at daemon start is test/plugin/enum-refusal-daemon-start-set.ci:
# the runner compares one exit code per test, the foreground daemon's
# (internal/test/runner/record.go, ExitCode), so each start is its own test.
#
# Leaf: bgp peer <name> session capability route-refresh, typedef
#   capability-mode (internal/component/bgp/yang/ze-bgp-conf.yang).
#
# Producers: cmd/ze/hub/main.go ("error: load config: %v"), the loader's
# "parse config: " (internal/component/config/line_error.go parseConfigError,
# built in loader.go), the parser refusal
# (internal/component/config/parser_diagnostics.go).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-config-enum-refusal-proposes-valid-values AC-10 (start).
# PREVENTS: `parse config: parse config:`, `line N: line N:`, `invalid enum`,
#   a start that reaches the peers, or a start refusal whose fix is not the
#   line the operator writes.
#
# Nothing reaches the wire: the daemon refuses the file before the reactor is
# built, so no peer process is started.

stdin=hier:terminator=EOF_HIER
bgp {
	router-id 203.0.113.253
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			capability {
				route-refresh requre
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_HIER

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=hier:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=error: load config: parse config: line 19: bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh: "requre" is not an accepted value (did you mean require?)
expect=stderr:pattern=route-refresh accepts only these values:\n +enable   Advertise the capability; no enforcement\n +disable  Do not advertise the capability; no enforcement\n +require  Advertise the capability; refuse the session when the peer does not offer it\n +refuse   Do not advertise the capability; refuse the session when the peer offers it\n *fix: route-refresh require;
reject=stderr:contains=bgp peers started
reject=stderr:pattern=parse config: parse config
reject=stderr:pattern=line [0-9]+: line [0-9]+
reject=stderr:pattern=invalid enum
reject=stderr:pattern=expected one of
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
